Well I started the game on Friday 13 and it seemingly showed in at least one
aspect: there were only 3 shops total, excluding minetown.

Pretty normal beginning.
Teetered on the brink of starvation a couple of times.
No bag of holding in minetown or sokoban, decided to use my magic lamp to get
one and luckily did. There were only 6 candles to be had, so I had to burn a
wish for candles, but that was ok, as I had so many wishes that I ended up
wishing for things such as cursed potions of confusions. I didn't even wrest the
last wish from my 2nd wand of wishing.
No bones files.
Got mojo at some point.
Used my amulet of reflection from sokoban to kill medusa, then got sheild of
reflection from statue of Perseus. I was planning on holding off on twoweaponing
for awhile so decided to try for grey dragon scale mail, but settled for black
and took my chances until I would get wand of wishing at castle. When I did get
the wand I got a cloak of magic resistance. At this point I was either using
shield and one weaponing, or wearing amulet of reflection and twoweaponing,
until I decided to use wish for SDSM(either that or use wish for scroll of
enchant armor, or blank scrolls as I had silver scales), and amulet of life
saving.
Decided to try to kill all major demons.
Made a few mistakes due to anxiety/excitement because it was my first time in
many situations of the endgame:
I killed Yendor! Got the book! Started franticly rushing upstairs... Oops! got
to get amulet first, duh! I think the line "You *do* have the *real* Amulet of
Yendor, don't you?" from maniacs ascention guide jarred my memory.
Lost a bag of holding, I think I put an unidentified wand of cancelation(one of
the few items left unidentified) in it while burdened and running away from
Rodney, after being so carefull up until then. This caused much distress as a
doubled back looking for it because at the time I only noticed when I went to
put something in and it wasn't there. I dont' think Rodney stole it because I
checked his corpse every time. I realized it wasn't worth getting this upset
about it and stopped looking for it, it was my secondary bag, and I think I had
emptied it recently.
Licked wounds at covienient alter directly above medusa.
Was extremely nervous about going upstairs at level one. Do I have to put it on?
Will that kill me? Oh well, I'll just go up... whew! Elemental planes very
strange! Almost starved to death on one plane, just because of the excitement, I
wasn't paying attention, whew, got ration out of bag and was able to nibble
between pummelings. Decided to go for the one tame angel deal, and decided to go
for Famine first. Got him a few times, went for the center alter. I think this
is it, I think the monsters are scared. Drop amulet on alter... nope, try it
with it just in inventory...

